# Copy to .env.local for local overrides. This project has no required secrets;
# public-facing identifiers are hardcoded because they must appear in the browser
# bundle anyway.
#
# Documented identifiers:
#   Prismic repository: reddoor-la  (see slicemachine.config.json)
#   Cloudflare Turnstile site key: 0x4AAAAAAAh2fGW6xIcdsqNr  (public, OK in client)
#   Google Analytics ID: G-2CZMPGL9RR  (public, OK in client)
#
# Content-migration secret (NOT needed for normal dev):
#   PRISMIC_WRITE_TOKEN=...   # used by the scripts/portfolio-intro/ migration
#                             # scripts (migrate.mjs, list-projects.mjs) via
#                             # `node --env-file=.env.local` — see that dir's README

# Inquiry-funnel secrets (the industry landing pages and /schedule):
#   FORMS_INGEST_URL / FORMS_INGEST_TOKEN
#       Central form ingest — the source of record for a lead. /api/inquiry
#       returns 500 without them; /api/book only skips the notification.
#
#   CRM_FUNNEL_ACTIVE_TOKEN=...
#       GoHighLevel location-level Private Integration Token, read by
#       /api/inquiry, /api/slots and /api/book. Unset, the CRM sync is skipped
#       with a warning (the lead still reaches ingest) and booking returns 500.
#       Needs exactly six scopes — anything broader is a liability, since this
#       one is deployed:
#           contacts.write            upsert, notes, tags, DND, outcome fields
#           contacts.readonly         finding a contact by email (see below)
#           opportunities.readonly    the dedupe lookup before creating a card
#           opportunities.write       the pipeline card
#           calendars.readonly        free-slots
#           calendars/events.write    creating, moving and cancelling appointments
#       contacts.readonly was added 2026-08-18. The inquiry and booking flows do
#       not need it — the upsert returns the contact — but /email/unsubscribed
#       and /meeting-outcome do: both take a TYPED email address from a form, so
#       without a lookup they would have to upsert, and an upsert invents a
#       contact for a typo. Neither a subscriber nor a call outcome should ever
#       be conjured out of a mistyped address.
#
#   CRM_CLAUDE_TOKEN=...
#       A separate, broader token for local investigation only. Deliberately
#       NOT the one the app reads, so a permissive token can never be the one
#       that ships. Nothing in src/ references it.
#
#   MEETING_OUTCOME_KEY=...
#       Shared key guarding /meeting-outcome, the internal page that records a
#       call's outcome against a contact. Unlike every other endpoint here, that
#       one writes a sales outcome onto somebody ELSE's record and can trigger
#       an email to them, so it is not left open the way the GHL page it
#       replaces is. Unset, the endpoint refuses everything — it fails closed.
#       The value rides in the "Client Meeting Status Update" trigger link as
#       ?k=<key>.
